# Let's try a smarter approach using the structure of QG3 quasigroups
# QG3 quasigroups have special structure related to Steiner triple systems

# For QG3: x[x[i][j]][x[j][i]] = i
# Combined with idempotent: x[i][i] = i
# This means if we set a = x[i][j] and b = x[j][i], then x[a][b] = i

